00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:54.500
Here's one,

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.033
a shape puzzle!

00:05:56.033 --> 00:05:58.033
Which shape comes next?

00:05:58.033 --> 00:05:58.533
A.

00:05:58.533 --> 00:05:59.533
A pentagon,

00:05:59.533 --> 00:06:00.033
B.

00:06:00.033 --> 00:06:01.067
A circle,

00:06:01.067 --> 00:06:01.567
C.

00:06:01.567 --> 00:06:02.567
A hexagon,

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:03.567
or D.

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:04.567
A square?

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:05.567
Five seconds!

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:12.567
TIME'S UP!

00:06:13.233 --> 00:06:14.667
The answer is...

00:06:14.667 --> 00:06:15.167
A,

00:06:15.167 --> 00:06:16.133
a pentagon!

00:06:16.133 --> 00:06:19.033
The sides count down by one:

00:06:19.033 --> 00:06:20.000
octagon eight,

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:20.967
heptagon seven,

00:06:20.967 --> 00:06:21.933
hexagon six,

00:06:21.933 --> 00:06:24.833
so next is the pentagon with

00:06:24.833 --> 00:06:25.800
five sides.

00:06:26.933 --> 00:06:28.267
Check this out,

00:06:28.267 --> 00:06:30.067
fill in the blank!

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:32.767
The museum guide gave such a

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:35.433
blank talk that nobody in the

00:06:35.433 --> 00:06:37.700
group wanted it to end.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:38.133
A.

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:38.567
Boring,

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:39.033
B.

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:39.467
Quiet,

00:06:39.467 --> 00:06:39.933
C.

00:06:39.933 --> 00:06:40.367
Short,

00:06:40.367 --> 00:06:41.267
or D.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:41.733
Fascinating?

00:06:41.733 --> 00:06:42.600
Five seconds!

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.600
TIME'S UP!

00:06:50.267 --> 00:06:50.767
It's...

00:06:50.767 --> 00:06:51.233
D,

00:06:51.233 --> 00:06:51.733
fascinating!

00:06:51.733 --> 00:06:54.700
If nobody wanted the talk to

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:55.167
